      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n\n## Column Mapping\n- courses: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER\n- Mathematics department: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- average for Mathematics department courses in the same academic year: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- course number: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- subject title: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- academic year: ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- row number within each academic year group ordered by course number: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER, ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- degree-granting department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject code: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE\n- subject code description: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC\n- average ASCII value of course number: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- variance of ASCII value of course number: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Question\nFor courses offered by the Mathematics department with at least 5 enrolled students, where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average for Mathematics department courses in the same academic year, show the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, and the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number. For each such course, also show the name of the degree-granting department, the subject code, the subject code description, and the average and variance of the ASCII values of the course numbers for that subject code, listing the columns in this order: course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, row number, department name, subject code, subject code description, average ASCII value of course number, and variance of ASCII value of course number. Do not return any rounded answers."
