      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 15, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2210\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code in degree-granting departments where the department is Mathematics, and for subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, rank of the subject code within each school name group ordered by subject code, subject ID, subject number, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the subject description from the CIS course catalog, ordered by school name, rank, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3248\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2365\", \"desc\": \"For the top 3 most frequently offered courses in the Mathematics department, for each course and each term it was offered, display the course number, course description, subject title, number of times offered, department name, number of unique course descriptions for that course and department, the minimum CIP program code for that course and department, the term code, the term description, the school name, and the department phone number. Do not repeat the course number if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by course number and term code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4658\", \"desc\": \"Show the Mathematics department courses with at least 5 enrolled students, including the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number, the term start date, calendar date, day of week, the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, and for each course, also display the responsible faculty name and the offer school name, but only for academic terms where the term status is 'Previous'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1427\", \"desc\": \"For each course in the Mathematics department that is degree granting and has a course level of 'G', show the course description, department name, school name, the administrative department name, and the dense rank over the administrative department name ordered by the administrative department name. Additionally, for each administrative department name, include a grand total of the number of such courses in the format of (null, null, null, administrative department name, null, total courses). Also, show the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics department subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021, along with the department name and term description (with all other columns as null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2398\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3237\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4229\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects in the \\\"Mathematics\\\" category, show the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, activity description, and the row number within each enrollment type group ordered by activity title, along with the academic year, department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, department phone number, and school name for each academic year and department where the IAP subject's term matches a department's fall term subject offering with more than 0 enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2335\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4756\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3393\", \"desc\": \"For subjects with at least 5 enrolled students that are offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, number of enrolled students, term code, material status key, ISBN, row number within each material status group ordered by subject ID, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, ordered by offering department name, material status key, and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1766\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
