    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database is returning an authentication error (access denied) on every attempt — this is an environment-level connection issue, not a query issue. I've retried multiple times. I'll construct the SQL strictly following the verified precedent patterns (dw_4584, dw_4658 for the inner CTE + yearly-average filter shape; dw_3356/dw_2224 for the SIS_DEPARTMENT/SIS_SUBJECT_CODE degree-granting join shape) and the provided hints.\n\n# Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: subjects offered per term in library reserve scope; one row per subject per term. Key columns: COURSE_NUMBER, SUBJECT_TITLE, OFFER_DEPT_NAME (e.g. 'Mathematics'), NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, TERM_CODE.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: term dimension; TERM_CODE, TERM_DESCRIPTION, ACADEMIC_YEAR, TERM_STATUS.\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT**: department dimension; DEPARTMENT_CODE, DEPARTMENT_NAME, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING ('Y'/'N').\n- **SIS_SUBJECT_CODE**: subject code lookup; COURSE_NUMBER, SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC, DEPARTMENT_CODE. Granularity: one row per subject code/course number.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE ↔ ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE (documented in column defs and used in dw_4584/dw_4658).\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE (documented; used in dw_3356, dw_2224).\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER ↔ SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER (per hint join keys).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences / Fitness\n- **Enrollment measure**: column_concept_enrollment_measures documents NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (library headcount) vs SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (registrar). The question's \"enrolled students\" maps to LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per hint and precedents dw_4584/dw_4658 — SUPPORTED.\n- **Term dimension**: ACADEMIC_TERMS (status-tracked) vs ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (superset, no status). No term-status filter is required here; hint specifies ACADEMIC_TERMS — SUPPORTED.\n- **Department name**: OFFER_DEPT_NAME (offering dept, used for the 'Mathematics' filter per precedents) vs SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME (requested output \"degree-granting department name\") — both used in their respective roles per the hint mapping.\n- **Precedent usage**: dw_4584 is the exact same-shape precedent (Mathematics, ≥5 enrolled, ROW_NUMBER within ACADEMIC_YEAR ordered by COURSE_NUMBER, filter NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > yearly average computed over Mathematics courses with ≥5 enrolled). Its AvgEnrolled CTE includes the ≥5 filter and the row number is computed before the average filter — I follow both conventions.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nThe inner-CTE + AvgEnrolled pattern serves \"above yearly average enrollment\" questions (dw_4584); SIS_SUBJECT_CODE→SIS_DEPARTMENT with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y' serves degree-granting department attribution (dw_3356, dw_2224, dw_4812).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nInvestigated: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, ACADEMIC_TERMS, SIS_DEPARTMENT, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (semantic_get); dw_4658, dw_4584, dw_3311, dw_3356, dw_2224 (semantic_get); concepts concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_department_dimension and column concepts enrollment_measures/department_name/term_code/year_columns (via search descriptions). mysql_query verification was impossible — persistent \"Access denied\" authentication error on every attempt (environment issue).\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n6a. Use LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (COURSE_NUMBER, SUBJECT_TITLE, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, OFFER_DEPT_NAME filter) joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS (TERM_DESCRIPTION, ACADEMIC_YEAR), then to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE_NUMBER, then to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT_CODE with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'. ASCII stats per SUBJECT_CODE computed in a grouped CTE over SIS_SUBJECT_CODE using AVG(ASCII(COURSE_NUMBER)) and VARIANCE(ASCII(COURSE_NUMBER)).\n\n6b. Three CTEs: inner_cte (Mathematics, ≥5 enrolled, ROW_NUMBER partitioned by ACADEMIC_YEAR ordered by COURSE_NUMBER — following dw_4584), AvgEnrolled (yearly average over the same filtered population — following dw_4584), SubjectCodeStats (per-subject-code ASCII avg/variance). Final filter: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > avg_enrolled.\n\n6c. Data: granularity of SIS_SUBJECT_CODE is one row per subject code/course number, so the COURSE_NUMBER join doesn't fan out materially; ASCII stats are pre-aggregated per SUBJECT_CODE to avoid fan-out. Semantic-network: all joins are documented edges. Business: exact precedent dw_4584 for the window/average shape.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_956e35cf260549e788d01504",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte AS (\\n    SELECT t0.COURSE_NUMBER,\\n           t0.SUBJECT_TITLE,\\n           t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS,\\n           t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION,\\n           t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR ORDER BY t0.COURSE_NUMBER) AS window_column\\n    FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0\\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\\n      AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 5\\n),\\nAvgEnrolled AS (\\n    SELECT t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n           AVG(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled\\n    FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0\\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\\n      AND t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 5\\n    GROUP BY t1.ACADEMIC_YEAR\\n),\\nSubjectCodeStats AS (\\n    SELECT SUBJECT_CODE,\\n           AVG(ASCII(COURSE_NUMBER)) AS avg_ascii_course_number,\\n           VARIANCE(ASCII(COURSE_NUMBER)) AS var_ascii_course_number\\n    FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\\n    GROUP BY SUBJECT_CODE\\n)\\nSELECT i.COURSE_NUMBER,\\n       i.SUBJECT_TITLE,\\n       i.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS,\\n       i.TERM_DESCRIPTION,\\n       i.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n       i.window_column,\\n       d.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n       s.SUBJECT_CODE,\\n       s.SUBJECT_CODE_DESC,\\n       scs.avg_ascii_course_number,\\n       scs.var_ascii_course_number\\nFROM inner_cte i\\nJOIN AvgEnrolled a ON i.ACADEMIC_YEAR = a.ACADEMIC_YEAR\\nJOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s ON i.COURSE_NUMBER = s.COURSE_NUMBER\\nJOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT d ON s.DEPARTMENT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE\\nJOIN SubjectCodeStats scs ON s.SUBJECT_CODE = scs.SUBJECT_CODE\\nWHERE i.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > a.avg_enrolled\\n  AND d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
